<ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/siege-of-jerusalem-1099"><span class="enc-name">Siege of Jerusalem (1099)</span><span class="enc-type">Siege · 1099</span><span class="enc-snip">The Siege of Jerusalem in 1099 was the capture of Jerusalem by the armies of the First Crusade, followed by a massacre of many of its inhabitants.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/siege-of-jerusalem-1187"><span class="enc-name">Siege of Jerusalem (1187)</span><span class="enc-type">Siege · 1187</span><span class="enc-snip">The Siege of Jerusalem in 1187 was the recapture of Jerusalem by Saladin after his victory over the Crusaders at Hattin.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/siege-of-jerusalem-587-bce"><span class="enc-name">Siege of Jerusalem (587 BCE)</span><span class="enc-type">Siege · 587 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Siege of Jerusalem in 587 BCE was the capture and destruction of Jerusalem by the Chaldean (Neo-Babylonian) king Nebuchadnezzar II.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/siege-of-jerusalem-597-bce"><span class="enc-name">Siege of Jerusalem (597 BCE)</span><span class="enc-type">Siege · 597 BCE</span><span class="enc-snip">The Siege of Jerusalem in 597 BCE was the capture of Jerusalem by Nebuchadnezzar II of the Chaldean Empire after the kingdom of Judah rebelled.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/siege-of-kawagoe-castle"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/siege-of-kawagoe-castle.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Siege of Kawagoe Castle</span><span class="enc-type">Battle · Siege · 1545–1546</span><span class="enc-snip">The Siege of Kawagoe Castle was a battle of Japan's Sengoku period in which the Later Hojo clan defended Kawagoe Castle in Musashi province against a large coalition of…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/siege-of-kerman"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/siege-of-kerman.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Siege of Kerman</span><span class="enc-type">Siege · 1794</span><span class="enc-snip">The Siege of Kerman was the final siege in 1794 in which the Qajar leader Agha Mohammad Khan captured the city of Kerman from Lotf Ali Khan, the last Zand ruler.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/siege-of-multan-1818"><span class="enc-name">Siege of Multan (1818)</span><span class="enc-type">Siege · 1818</span><span class="enc-snip">The Siege of Multan in 1818 was the capture of the city of Multan from its Afghan governor by the forces of Ranjit Singh.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/siege-of-odawara-1590"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/siege-of-odawara-1590.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Siege of Odawara (1590)</span><span class="enc-type">Siege · 1590</span><span class="enc-snip">The Siege of Odawara of 1590 was Toyotomi Hideyoshi's campaign against the Later Hojo clan, whose refusal to submit was the last obstacle to his unification of Japan.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/siege-of-orleans"><span class="enc-name">Siege of Orléans</span><span class="enc-type">Siege · 1428–1429</span><span class="enc-snip">The Siege of Orléans was the English siege of the city of Orléans on the Loire from October 1428 to May 1429, during the Hundred Years' War.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/siege-of-osaka"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/siege-of-osaka.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Siege of Osaka</span><span class="enc-type">Siege · 1614–1615</span><span class="enc-snip">The Siege of Osaka was a series of campaigns in 1614–1615 in which the forces of Tokugawa Ieyasu attacked Osaka Castle, held by the Toy