was the last major battle of the American Revolutionary War.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/siege-tower"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/siege-tower.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Siege tower</span><span class="enc-type">Term</span><span class="enc-snip">A siege tower is a mobile wooden tower used to bring attackers to the top of fortification walls.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/siege-warfare"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/siege-warfare.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Siege warfare</span><span class="enc-type">Term</span><span class="enc-snip">Siege warfare is the conduct of military operations to capture or defend fortified places, through blockade, assault, mining or bombardment.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/siegen"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/siegen.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Siegen</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Siegen is a university city in North Rhine-Westphalia, Germany, on the Sieg in the Siegerland.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/siegerland"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/siegerland.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Siegerland</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Siegerland is a hilly region around the upper Sieg river in the south of North Rhine-Westphalia, centred on Siegen.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/siegfried-of-westerburg"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/siegfried-of-westerburg.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Siegfried of Westerburg</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span>