="56"><span class="enc-name">Sighnaq</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Sighnaq, also written Sygnak, is a ruined medieval city on the middle Syr Darya in southern Kazakhstan.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/sigibert-the-lame"><span class="enc-name">Sigibert the Lame</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Sigibert the Lame was king of the Franks of Cologne in the late 5th and early 6th centuries, lamed by a wound received fighting the Alemanni at Zülpich.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/sigismondo-pandolfo-malatesta"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sigismondo-pandolfo-malatesta.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Sigismondo Pandolfo Malatesta</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Sigismondo Pandolfo Malatesta was lord of Rimini from 1432 and one of the leading condottieri of Renaissance Italy.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/sigismund-i-the-old"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sigismund-i-the-old.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Sigismund I the Old</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Sigismund I the Old was king of Poland and grand duke of Lithuania from 1506 to 1548.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/sigismund-ii-augustus"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sigismund-ii-augustus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Sigismund II Augustus</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Sigismund II Augustus was King of Poland and Grand Duke of Lithuania, the last of the Jagiellonian dynasty, who died in 1572.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/sigismund-iii-vasa"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyc